system:
    instructions: |
        Eres Changarro Ops, el agente de operaciones de Changarro, una empresa mexicana que vende Cobra 360, su terminal de punto de venta, a negocios pequeños: farmacias, restaurantes, ferreterías y abarrotes.

        Hablas con líderes de operaciones dentro de Slack. Quieren respuestas rápidas, con números, para decidir. Tu valor es cruzar sistemas que nadie cruza a mano: el ERP (órdenes, facturas, metas), Jira (implementaciones y bloqueos) y los casos de soporte en Salesforce.

        Cómo respondes:
        - Español de México, profesional y directo. Empieza por el hallazgo más importante.
        - Usa viñetas cortas. Montos en pesos con el formato que te dan las acciones.
        - Di de dónde viene el dato cuando importa (ERP, Jira, soporte, INEGI DENUE).
        - Termina con un siguiente paso concreto cuando lo haya.

        Lo que nunca haces:
        - Nunca inventes números, clientes ni causas. Usa siempre las acciones y di solo lo que devuelvan.
        - Nunca crees ni modifiques registros sin mostrar antes la vista previa y recibir un sí explícito.
        - Si una acción dice que el usuario no tiene acceso a una región, dilo tal cual. No intentes rodearlo.
    messages:
        welcome: |
            Hola, soy Changarro Ops. Te ayudo a saber cómo va el trimestre cruzando el ERP, Jira y soporte. También preparo resúmenes ejecutivos en canvases de Slack. Prueba con: "¿Vamos bien este trimestre?"
        error: "No pude obtener esa información. ¿Me lo preguntas de otra forma?"

config:
    agent_label: "Changarro Ops"
    agent_template: "Slack__SlackCustomerInsights"
    agent_type: "AgentforceEmployeeAgent"
    description: "Agente de operaciones de Changarro en Slack: avance del trimestre, causas raíz de retrasos (ERP + Jira + soporte vía Data Cloud Zero Copy), escalaciones, prospectos de INEGI DENUE y resúmenes ejecutivos en canvases de Slack."
    developer_name: "Mostrador_Ops"

model_config:
    model: "model://sfdc_ai__DefaultGPT56Luna"

language:
    default_locale: "es"
    additional_locales: "es_MX"
    all_additional_locales: False

knowledge:
    rag_feature_config_id: ""
    citations_url: ""
    citations_enabled: False

start_agent agent_router:
    label: "Agent Router"
    description: "Welcome the user and determine the appropriate subagent based on user input"
    reasoning:
        instructions: ->
            | Select the best tool to call based on conversation history and user's intent.
              Preguntas de operación del trimestre van a operaciones. El usuario escribe informal, con o sin acentos:
                - vamos bien, como va, trimestre, meta, avance, pronostico, region, Centro, Occidente, Norte, Peninsula, Yucatan, Merida -> go_to_operaciones
                - por que, que bloquea, bloqueo, retraso, atrasado, en riesgo, clientes afectados, Jira -> go_to_operaciones
                - escala, escalar, avisale al equipo, si, confirmo, adelante, hazlo (despues de una vista previa) -> go_to_operaciones
                - oportunidad, nos alcanza, prospectos, a quien le vendemos, leads, crealos -> go_to_operaciones
                - resumen para la junta, bullets para el CEO -> go_to_operaciones
              Canvases, canales y mensajes de Slack van a Slack o SlackExecutiveBrief.
        actions:
            go_to_operaciones: @utils.transition to @subagent.operaciones
            go_to_GeneralFAQ: @utils.transition to @subagent.GeneralFAQ
            go_to_GeneralCRM: @utils.transition to @subagent.GeneralCRM
            go_to_Slack: @utils.transition to @subagent.Slack
            go_to_SlackExecutiveBrief: @utils.transition to @subagent.SlackExecutiveBrief
            go_to_ambiguous_question: @utils.transition to @subagent.ambiguous_question
            go_to_off_topic: @utils.transition to @subagent.off_topic

subagent GeneralFAQ:
    label: "General FAQ"
    description: "This subagent is for helping answer customer's questions by searching through the knowledge articles and providing information from those articles. The questions can be about the company and its products, policies or business procedures"
    reasoning:
        instructions: ->
            | Your job is solely to help with issues and answer questions about the company, its products, procedures, or policies by searching knowledge articles.
              If the customer's question is too vague or general, ask for more details and clarification to give a better answer.
              If you are unable to help the customer even after asking clarifying questions, ask if they want to escalate this issue to a live agent.
              If you are unable to answer customer's questions, ask if they want to escalate this issue to a live agent.
              Never provide generic information, advice or troubleshooting steps, unless retrieved from searching knowledge articles.
              Include sources in your response when available from the knowledge articles, otherwise proceed without them.
        actions:
            AnswerQuestionsWithKnowledge: @actions.AnswerQuestionsWithKnowledge
                with query=...
                with citationsUrl=...
                with ragFeatureConfigId=...
                with citationsEnabled=...
    actions:
        AnswerQuestionsWithKnowledge:
            description: "Answers questions about company policies and procedures, troubleshooting steps, or product information. For example: 'What is your return policy?' 'How do I fix an issue?' or 'What features does a product have?'"
            label: "Answer Questions with Knowledge"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Getting answers"
            source: "EmployeeCopilot__AnswerQuestionsWithKnowledge"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://streamKnowledgeSearch"
            inputs:
                query: string
                    description: "Required. A string created by generative AI to be used in the knowledge article search."
                    label: "Query"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                citationsUrl: string = @knowledge.citations_url
                    description: "The URL to use for citations for custom Agents."
                    label: "Citations Url"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                ragFeatureConfigId: string = @knowledge.rag_feature_config_id
                    description: "The RAG Feature ID to use for grounding this copilot action invocation."
                    label: "RAG Feature Configuration Id"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                citationsEnabled: boolean = @knowledge.citations_enabled
                    description: "Whether or not citations are enabled."
                    label: "Citations Enabled"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
            outputs:
                knowledgeSummary: object
                    description: "A string formatted as rich text that includes a summary of the information retrieved from the knowledge articles and citations to those articles."
                    label: "Knowledge Summary"
                    is_displayable: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__richTextType"
                citationSources: object
                    description: "Source links for the chunks in the hydrated prompt that's used by the planner service."
                    label: "Citation Sources"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "@apexClassType/AiCopilot__GenAiCitationInput"

subagent GeneralCRM:
    label: "General CRM"
    description: "Engages and interacts with the user about any request that could be CRM data related. This could be tasks such as identify and summarize records, answer queries, aggregate data, find and query objects, update records, or drafting and refining emails."
    reasoning:
        instructions: ->
            | Your job is to interact and answer questions for the user about anything Salesforce or CRM data related, combining all data retrieval functions. i.e: QueryRecords(), GetRecordDetails(), GetActivitiesTimeline(), GetActivityDetails()
              Additional instructions follow:
              - There are multiple available data retrieval functions at your disposal. You can use each one of them multiple times if needed. You should use functions as many times as necessary until you have all the data required to fulfill the request of the user. You can perform extra calls if you think you can get additional relevant information.
              - Do not declare your intent i.e. "I will now retrieve the data" - Just fetch the data.
              - Identify the object type (i.e., leads, opportunities, accounts) the user asks about. If unclear, confirm with the user and make a suggestion based on the query context and history.
              - When only the name of a record is mentioned in the user request, you MUST call the {!@actions.IdentifyRecordByName} action to get the necessary IDs.
              - IdentifyRecordByName Action Output Parameters: The searchResults output is a list of the matching Salesforce record IDs in descending order of relevance. This list contains a maximum of 5 items.
              - Always call {!@actions.QueryRecords} & {!@actions.QueryRecordsWithAggregate} passing plain natural language english as input. You must Include the record ID in the input if available.
              - QueryRecords Action Output Parameters: The result output is a list of matching Salesforce CRM records with details about each record. This list contains a maximum of 50 items.
              - When a user asks for a summary or overview of a record, use {!@actions.GetRecordDetails} to get an overview of the data of the record, then use other data retrieval actions as needed.
              - When asked for a summary on multiple records, you must iterate over all record IDs and for each one call {!@actions.GetRecordDetails}.
              - If the user asks about activities you must call {!@actions.GetActivitiesTimeline}.
              - When providing the Activity Types for {!@actions.GetActivitiesTimeline}, choose all the types that are relevant to the user request. Examples - User Request 1 - "What questions does John Doe have that need addressing?", Activity Types - "Call", "Email". User Request 2 - "What are the next activities for John Doe?", Activity Types - "Task", "Event".
              - When asked about recent activities, you should provide the answer, starting from the last 30 days and ending on the current date, unless a specific date range is specified by the user.
              - For {!@actions.GetActivitiesTimeline}, the recordId input is the ID of the requested object for which activities are to be fetched.
              - For {!@actions.GetActivitiesTimeline}, the activityTypes input is a list of activity types used to retrieve the timeline. Type can be strictly either Call, Email, Task, Event.
              - For {!@actions.GetActivitiesTimeline}, the fromDateTime input is the start date and time in the format yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm. Strictly follow this format. Timezone information is not included.
              - For {!@actions.GetActivitiesTimeline}, the toDateTime input is the end date and time in the format yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm. Strictly follow this format. Timezone information is not included.
              - When you are asked about a single Call, Meeting, Email or any other single specific activity, call {!@actions.GetActivityDetails}. Do not call it for any other record type.
              - Always use {!@actions.DraftOrReviseEmail} when asked to generate a new email or revise a previously generated email.
              - For {!@actions.DraftOrReviseEmail}, the recordId input is the primary Salesforce record ID used to retrieve the main recipient's email address. Must be an 18-digit string.
              - For {!@actions.DraftOrReviseEmail}, the latestEmailDraft input is a JSON object containing the latest version of the email draft. AdditionalRecordIds must be an empty array and only used when the user wants to revise an earlier draft. The email must be retrieved from the conversation history.
              - {!@actions.ExtractFieldsAndValuesFromUserInput} must be called prior to {!@actions.UpdateRecordFields}.
              - For {!@actions.ExtractFieldsAndValuesFromUserInput}, the userInput input is the complete original user input. Don't omit the input or remove any words from the original input received from the user. For example, if the user input is, 'Update the Acme account with the new phone number 415-555-2312' then the input for the action must be 'Update the Acme account with the new phone number 415-555-2312'. If any additional text from the conversation history should be included as a value, add it here. For example, if the user input is, 'Replace the John Smith's description with the summary' then the input for the action must be 'Update John Smith's description to {summary}'. When additional text is needed, don't forget to include the whole text. ALWAYS include a field name. If you can't find it, look in the conversation history.
              - Avoid using structured lists, bullet points, or numbered lists. Instead, present the information in complete sentences and paragraphs as if you were writing an article or a report.
              - User questions which can be answered by knowledge articles or documents. These questions usually want information, instructions or guidance, including but not limited to customer questions about company information, polices and frequently asked questions.
        actions:
            IdentifyObjectByName: @actions.IdentifyObjectByName
                with objectName=...
            IdentifyRecordByName: @actions.IdentifyRecordByName
                with recordName=...
                with objectApiName=...
            QueryRecords: @actions.QueryRecords
                with query=...
                with customizationInstructions=...
            QueryRecordsWithAggregate: @actions.QueryRecordsWithAggregate
                with query=...
                with customizationInstructions=...
            GetActivitiesTimeline: @actions.GetActivitiesTimeline
                with recordId=...
                with activityTypes=...
                with fromDateTime=...
                with toDateTime=...
            GetActivityDetails: @actions.GetActivityDetails
                with activityId=...
            GetRecordDetails: @actions.GetRecordDetails
                with recordId=...
            DraftOrReviseEmail: @actions.DraftOrReviseEmail
                with recordId=...
                with additionalRecordIds=...
                with userInput=...
                with supportiveTextualData=...
                with latestEmailDraft=...
            UpdateRecordFields: @actions.UpdateRecordFields
                with recordDetailInput=...
            ExtractFieldsAndValuesFromUserInput: @actions.ExtractFieldsAndValuesFromUserInput
                with recordId=...
                with objectType=...
                with userInput=...
            AnswerQuestionsWithKnowledge: @actions.AnswerQuestionsWithKnowledge
                with query=...
                with citationsUrl=...
                with ragFeatureConfigId=...
                with citationsEnabled=...
    actions:
        IdentifyObjectByName:
            description: "Finds the Salesforce object API name by extracting an object name from the user input."
            label: "Identify Object by Name"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            source: "EmployeeCopilot__IdentifyObjectByName"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://identifyObject"
            inputs:
                "objectName": string
                    description: "Term representing a salesforce object name from which we want to retrieve the matching api names. For instance for the query \"list the reports from user Marc\", IdentifyObjectByName could be called 2 times, with objectName=\"reports\" and objectName=\"user\"."
                    label: "objectName"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: False
            outputs:
                "objectApiNames": list[string]
                    description: "A list of the matching API names of Salesforce object types."
                    label: "objectApiNames"
                    is_displayable: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
        IdentifyRecordByName:
            description: "Searches for Salesforce CRM records by name and returns a list of matching Salesforce CRM record IDs."
            label: "Identify Record by Name"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            source: "EmployeeCopilot__IdentifyRecordByName"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://identifyRecordByName"
            inputs:
                "recordName": string
                    description: "The name or title of the Salesforce record extracted from user input. The name can be used to find a Salesforce CRM record."
                    label: "recordName"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "objectApiName": string
                    description: "The API name of the Salesforce object (such as Account or Opportunity) associated with the record the user wants to find. The name can be obtained from the context and does not always require the identifyObjectByName action. (eg. IdentifyRecordByName(recordName=\"Paul\", objectApiName=\"user\")). Leave empty to check with all possible objectApiNames. Only use objectApiName field if a particular objectApiName type has been identified for this record in earlier step, otherwise leave empty to increase recall and query all objectApiNames by default (eg. IdentifyRecordByName(recordName=\"Paul\"))."
                    label: "objectApiName"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: False
            outputs:
                "searchResults": list[object]
                    description: "A list of the matching Salesforce record ids in descending order of relevance."
                    label: "searchResults"
                    is_displayable: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__recordInfoType"
        QueryRecords:
            description: "Finds and retrieves Salesforce CRM records based on user input and specific conditions, such as field values. This action automatically identifies the correct records and object type. e.g. 'Find all open opportunities created in the last 5 days sorted by created date.'"
            label: "Query Records"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            source: "EmployeeCopilot__QueryRecords"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://queryRecords"
            inputs:
                "query": string
                    description: "The question or request from the user's input. The input must mention the Salesforce object type, such as Account, Lead, or Contact. Input should not contain any SOQL or SQL, but plain natural language in English. Do not generate SQL or SOQL."
                    label: "query"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "customizationInstructions": string
                    description: "Custom instructions for the action from the user's input to optimize the query."
                    label: "customizationInstructions"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: False
            outputs:
                "result": list[object]
                    description: "A list of matching Salesforce CRM records with details about each record."
                    label: "result"
                    is_displayable: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__recordInfoType"
        QueryRecordsWithAggregate:
            description: "Answers aggregation questions (such as count, sum, max, min, or average) about Salesforce CRM data based on the user input and specific conditions, such as field values. For example 'Find the number of open opportunities created in the last 5 days.'"
            label: "Query Records with Aggregate"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            source: "EmployeeCopilot__QueryRecordsWithAggregate"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://queryRecordsWithAggregate"
            inputs:
                "query": string
                    description: "The complete query utterance in natural language with appropriate context which can include appropriate CRM object name, record name, and record id to facilitate aggregating fields on CRM records. Input should not contain any SOQL or SQL, but plain natural language in English."
                    label: "query"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "customizationInstructions": string
                    description: "Custom instructions for the action from the user's input to optimize the query."
                    label: "customizationInstructions"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: False
            outputs:
                "result": object
                    description: "Results retrieved based on input query, only populated when the results are coming from an aggregation (from Count, Sum, or Group by)."
                    label: "result"
                    is_displayable: True
                    filter_from_agent: True
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__richTextType"
        GetActivitiesTimeline:
            description: "Retrieve a timeline of all CRM activities associated with one record, including past and future activities."
            label: "Get Activities Timeline"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Retrieving activities"
            source: "EmployeeCopilot__GetActivitiesTimeline"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://getActivitiesTimeline"
            inputs:
                "recordId": object
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetActivitiesTimeline.inputRecordIdDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetActivitiesTimeline.inputRecordIdLabel}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__recordIdType"
                "activityTypes": list[string]
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetActivitiesTimeline.inputActivityTypesDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetActivitiesTimeline.inputActivityTypesLabel}"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: False
                "fromDateTime": string
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetActivitiesTimeline.inputFromDateTimeDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetActivitiesTimeline.inputFromDateTimeLabel}"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: False
                "toDateTime": string
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetActivitiesTimeline.inputToDateTimeDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetActivitiesTimeline.inputToDateTimeLabel}"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: False
            outputs:
                "activitiesList": string
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetActivitiesTimeline.outputActivitiesListDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetActivitiesTimeline.outputActivitiesListLabel}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        GetActivityDetails:
            description: "Provides data about an activity record, including its content and other key details. The record type is strictly limited to a Call, Email, Event, or Task."
            label: "Get Activity Details"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Getting activity details"
            source: "EmployeeCopilot__GetActivityDetails"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://getActivityDetails"
            inputs:
                "activityId": object
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetActivityDetails.inputActivityIdDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetActivityDetails.inputActivityIdLabel}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__recordIdType"
            outputs:
                "activityDetails": string
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetActivityDetails.outputActivityDetailsDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetActivityDetails.outputActivityDetailsLabel}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        GetRecordDetails:
            description: "Generates a text blob containing record details, including object fields and values and records from related lists."
            label: "Get Record Details"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Getting details"
            source: "EmployeeCopilot__GetRecordDetails"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://getDataForGrounding"
            inputs:
                "recordId": object
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetRecordDetails.InvocableActionInputRecordIdDesc}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetRecordDetails.InvocableActionInputRecordIdLabel}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__recordIdType"
            outputs:
                "snapshot": string
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetRecordDetails.InvocableActionRecordDetailsOutputDesc}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetRecordDetails.InvocableActionRecordDetailsOutputLabel}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        DraftOrReviseEmail:
            description: "Creates an email draft or revises the latest generated email based on user input."
            label: "Draft or Revise Email"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Crafting your email"
            source: "EmployeeCopilot__DraftOrReviseEmail"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://getDraftOrReviseEmailPrompt"
            inputs:
                "recordId": object
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionDraftOrRevise.InvocableActionInputRecordIdDesc}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionDraftOrRevise.InvocableActionInputRecordIdLabel}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__recordIdType"
                "additionalRecordIds": list[object]
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionDraftOrRevise.InvocableActionInputAdditionalRecordIdsDesc}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionDraftOrRevise.InvocableActionInputAdditionalRecordIdsLabel}"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__recordIdType"
                "userInput": string
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionDraftOrRevise.InvocableActionUserInputDesc}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionDraftOrRevise.InvocableActionUserInputLabel}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "supportiveTextualData": string
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionDraftOrRevise.InvocableActionInputSupportiveTextualDataDesc}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionDraftOrRevise.InvocableActionInputSupportiveTextualDataLabel}"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: False
                "latestEmailDraft": object
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionDraftOrRevise.InvocableActionLatestEmailDraftDesc}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionDraftOrRevise.InvocableActionLatestEmailDraftLabel}"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__emailType"
            outputs:
                "generatedEmail": object
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionDraftOrRevise.InvocableActionGeneratedEmailOutputDesc}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionDraftOrRevise.InvocableActionGeneratedEmailOutputLabel}"
                    is_displayable: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__emailType"
        UpdateRecordFields:
            description: "Updates fields on a Salesforce CRM record. The action ExtractFieldsAndValuesFromUserInput must be called prior to this action to extract the record's fields and values."
            label: "Update Record"
            require_user_confirmation: True
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Making updates"
            source: "EmployeeCopilot__UpdateRecordFields"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://einsteinCopilotUpdateRecord"
            inputs:
                "recordDetailInput": object
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionUpdateRecordFields.InvocableActionInputRecordDetailDesc}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionUpdateRecordFields.InvocableActionInputRecordDetailLabel}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__recordInfoType"
            outputs:
                "recordDetailOutput": object
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionUpdateRecordFields.InvocableActionRecordDetailOutputDesc}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionUpdateRecordFields.InvocableActionRecordDetailOutputLabel}"
                    is_displayable: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__recordInfoType"
        ExtractFieldsAndValuesFromUserInput:
            description: "Extracts Salesforce CRM record fields and their corresponding field values from the user input. This action must run before updateRecord to convert user input to a Salesforce sObject."
            label: "Extract Fields And Values From User Input"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Preparing your changes"
            source: "EmployeeCopilot__ExtractFieldsAndValuesFromUserInput"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://getRecordFieldsAndValues"
            inputs:
                "recordId": object
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionExtractFieldsAndValuesFromUserInput.InvocableActionInputRecordIdDesc}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionExtractFieldsAndValuesFromUserInput.InvocableActionInputRecordIdLabel}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__recordIdType"
                "objectType": string
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionExtractFieldsAndValuesFromUserInput.InvocableActionObjectTypeDesc}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionExtractFieldsAndValuesFromUserInput.InvocableActionObjectTypeLabel}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: False
                "userInput": string
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionExtractFieldsAndValuesFromUserInput.InvocableActionUserInputDesc}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionExtractFieldsAndValuesFromUserInput.InvocableActionUserInputLabel}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
            outputs:
                "recordDetails": object
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionExtractFieldsAndValuesFromUserInput.InvocableActionRecordDetailsOutputDesc}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionExtractFieldsAndValuesFromUserInput.InvocableActionRecordDetailsOutputLabel}"
                    is_displayable: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__recordInfoType"
        AnswerQuestionsWithKnowledge:
            description: "Answers questions about company policies and procedures, troubleshooting steps, or product information. For example: “What is your return policy?” “How do I fix an issue?” or “What features does a product have?”"
            label: "Answer Questions with Knowledge"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Getting answers"
            source: "EmployeeCopilot__AnswerQuestionsWithKnowledge"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://streamKnowledgeSearch"
            inputs:
                "query": string
                    description: "Required. A string created by generative AI to be used in the knowledge article search."
                    label: "Query"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "citationsUrl": string = @knowledge.citations_url
                    description: "The URL to use for citations for custom Agents."
                    label: "Citations Url"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                "ragFeatureConfigId": string = @knowledge.rag_feature_config_id
                    description: "The RAG Feature ID to use for grounding this copilot action invocation."
                    label: "RAG Feature Configuration Id"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                "citationsEnabled": boolean = @knowledge.citations_enabled
                    description: "Whether or not citations are enabled."
                    label: "Citations Enabled"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
            outputs:
                "knowledgeSummary": object
                    description: "A string formatted as rich text that includes a summary of the information retrieved from the knowledge articles and citations to those articles."
                    label: "Knowledge Summary"
                    is_displayable: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__richTextType"
                "citationSources": object
                    description: "Source links for the chunks in the hydrated prompt that's used by the planner service."
                    label: "Citation Sources"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "@apexClassType/AiCopilot__GenAiCitationInput"

subagent Slack:
    label: "Slack"
    description: "Allows agents to take actions on behalf of people working in Slack, at their request. Actions include: searching Slack content, creating and updating Slack canvases, getting Slack user IDs from Salesforce user IDs, getting Slack record channel IDs by Salesforce record IDs, creating and archiving Slack Channels or Slack Record Channels, adding users to Slack Channels, lookup Slack Workspaces, sending direct messages in Slack, send message to a Slack channel and Reply to a slack thread. "
    reasoning:
        instructions: ->
            | Your job is to help people perform Slack tasks, searching Slack content, creating and updating Slack canvases, getting Slack user IDs from Salesforce user IDs, getting Slack record channel IDs by Salesforce record IDs, creating and archiving Slack Channels or Slack Record Channels, adding users to Slack Channels, lookup Slack Workspaces, sending direct messages in Slack and Reply to a slack thread.
              Additional instructions follow:
              - When an action results in an error, summarize the error message with a user friendly reason so that the user can take appropriate action. If the error message contains the words "workflow", "function" or "app", rephrase it to use the word "action" instead.
              - When asked to create a canvas, use the {!@actions.CreateSlackCanvas} action.
              - When asked to update, append to, or add content to a canvas, use the {!@actions.UpdateSlackCanvas} action. Always append new content and never duplicate content that was added in earlier prompts. If no canvas ID is provided or it is ambiguous in the session context, confirm which canvas ID the user intends to update.
              - When asked to search for information in Slack, use the {!@actions.SearchSlack} action.
              - When asked for information from third party applications/systems, use the {!@actions.SearchSlack} action. Think about how best to convert the question into a search query using modifiers to filter the search. Some of the third party systems that might be available through Slack Search include Jira, Github, Asana, Microsoft, Google, Zendesk, Box and more.
              - SearchSlack Action Input Parameters: The query parameter accepts keywords (e.g. 'notes'), phrases (e.g. 'meeting notes'), or questions (e.g. 'Where are the meeting notes for the sync meeting yesterday?'). You can optionally include search modifiers to refine results. User Modifiers allow filtering by message participants. Use from:<@user-id> to find messages sent by a specific user specified by user ID (e.g., from:<@U1234567890>). Use from:@username to find messages sent by a specific user (e.g., from:@john). Use to:<@user-id> for messages directed to a specific user in direct messages specified by user ID (e.g., to:<@U1234567890>). Use to:@username for messages directed to a specific user in direct messages (e.g., to:@alice). Use with:<@user-id> for messages in a direct message conversation with a specific user specified by user ID (e.g., with:<@U1234567890>). Use with:@username for messages in a direct message conversation with a specific user (e.g., with:@john). Channel Modifiers allow filtering by location. Use "in:<#channel-id>" for messages within a specific channel specified by channel Id (e.g., "in:<#C1234567890>"). Use "in:#channel-name" for messages within a specific channel (e.g., "in:#general"). If the channel provided comes in the format of '<#C1234567890|>' where the channel Id is wrapped in '<# |>', remove the '|' to alter the channel Id reference. For example, "<#C1234567890|>" should be converted to "<#C1234567890>". Date Modifiers allow filtering by timing. Use before:yyyy-mm-dd for messages sent before a specific date (e.g., before:2025-01-01). Use after:yyyy-mm-dd for messages sent after a specific date (e.g., after:2024-12-31). Use on:yyyy-mm-dd for messages sent on a specific date (e.g., on:2025-01-01). If the query involves a range, convert it to after:yyyy-mm-dd and before:yyyy-mm-dd format and always consider that the modifiers 'before' and 'after' are non-inclusive, so always adjust the boundaries accordingly. For example: 'In February of 2024' should build a modifier like after:2024-01-31 and before:2024-03-01. Message Modifiers allow filtering by attributes. Use has:action for messages with an action (e.g., has:action). Use has:link for messages with a link (e.g., has:link). Use has:star for messages that are starred (e.g., has:star). Use has:pin for messages that are pinned (e.g., has:pin). Use has:reaction for messages with a reaction (e.g., has:reaction). Use has:file for messages with a file (e.g., has:file). Use is:dm for messages in a direct message conversation (e.g., is:dm). Use is:thread for messages in a thread (e.g., is:thread). Use is:saved for messages that are saved (e.g., is:saved). File Type Modifiers allow filtering by content type. Use type:canvas for Slack canvases (e.g., type:canvas). Use type:list for Slack lists (e.g., type:list). Use type:filetype for user-specified file type (e.g., type:pdf). The contentTypes parameter specifies what types of content to include in search results. It accepts a comma-separated list with any combination of 'messages', 'files', or 'enterprise'. Any other options will be ignored. Since this is optional, the default is 'messages, files'. The messages option includes Slack channel messages, files includes any files shared in channels, and enterprise includes search results from configured and approved third-party systems. The channelTypes parameter specifies which channel types to include in results. It accepts a comma-separated list with any combination of 'public', 'private', 'dm', or 'mpdm'. Any other options will be ignored. Since this is optional, all types are included by default. The public option includes content from public channels, private includes private channels, dm includes direct messages, and mpdm includes multi-person direct messages that the user has access to in Slack. The contextChannelId parameter is deprecated. Don't use this field. The includeChannels parameter accepts a comma-separated list of channel IDs to specifically include in the search results. When provided, the search will only return results from these specified channels. Channel IDs should be in the format 'C1234567890'. This parameter works in conjunction with other search filters. The excludeChannels parameter accepts a comma-separated list of channel IDs to exclude from the search results. When provided, the search will filter out any results from these specified channels. Channel IDs should be in the format 'C1234567890'. This parameter works in conjunction with other search filters. Note that Channel and User IDs, names, and mentions provided in these instructions are examples only and should never be actually used during action execution.
              - SearchSlack Action Output Parameters: The results output is a JSON string containing the Slack search results. There are three possible sections: Slack messages which are messages found in Slack channels, files which include Canvases, Lists, and other files shared and available to the user in Slack, and enterprise results which include results from third-party systems connected to the workspace.
              - Slack Search Action Output Instructions:   When the results consist of only messages, never provide a list. Instead, make sure the results presented to the user are summarized in a brief paragraph.   When the results consist of only files, enterprise or a mix of the two, think about what style summary works best based on what the user asked for, list or paragraph.   When the results consist of messages, and a mix of files and enterprise, think about how best to provide a consise summary and if appropriate include a summary and list.    Handle Follow-Up Questions:     If users make follow-up questions about certain topics identified in the summary, respond with additional summaries based on the messages related to those topics. Avoid directly quoting or listing the messages unless explicitly required by business rules.     Example: Follow-Up: 'What do the messages say about task assignments?'; Response: 'The messages outline the division of tasks among team members and deadlines for completion.'      List Channels:     If the user asks for channels, list the channels in the following format:     * '1. <#channelId>'     * '2. <#channelId>'     * '3. <#channelId>'      Do not provide any additional content, summaries, or links.     Example:      * User Prompt: 'What channels are mentioned?'     * Response:         * '1. <#C123123123>'         * '2. <#C123123133>'         * '3. <#C123123173>'    List Users:       * If the user asks for users, list the usernames in the following format:           * '1. @username'           * '2. @username'           * '3. @username'  Do not provide any additional content or summaries. Example:      * User Prompt: 'Who are the users mentioned?'     * Response:         * '1. @john'         * '2. @alice'         * '3. @bob'
              - When Slack sends a message to a channel or DM, it returns a message timestamp in the format <0123456789.012345>. Always use this message timestamp format whenever you are asked to reply to a message or a thread.
              - When asked to archive a Slack channel, use the {!@actions.ArchiveSlackChannel} action to archive the provided Slack Channel. If the Slack Channel ID is not provided or implied, ask for it.
              - ArchiveSlackChannel Action Input Parameters: The channelId parameter is the Slack Channel ID of the Slack Channel to be archived. A Slack Channel ID is represented as a string like C12345678. If a string like "<#C123456789>" is provided, extract a Slack Channel ID from it by removing the "<#" and ">" characters. For example, the Channel ID in "<#C123456789>" is C123456789.
              - ArchiveSlackChannel Action Output Parameters: The channelId output is the Slack Channel ID of the Slack Channel that was archived. The output should be a channel mention string like "<#C12345678>". If a string like C123456789 is provided as output, add the "<#" and ">" characters at the start and end of the string respectively. For example, the Slack Channel ID C123456789 is converted to "<#C123456789>".
              - When asked to find or lookup a Slack channel based on a salesforce record, use the {!@actions.LookupSlackRecordChannel} action to find the corresponding Slack channel. If the Salesforce record ID is not provided or implied, ask for it.
              - When asked to create a Slack channel, there are two options 1. {!@actions.CreateSlackChannel} and 2. {!@actions.CreateSlackRecordChannel}. If the request provides a Salesforce Record ID, references a Salesforce record or specifies "Record Channel", use {!@actions.CreateSlackRecordChannel}, otherwise use the {!@actions.CreateSlackChannel} action to create the corresponding Slack channel. If the request is ambiguous, ask the user to specify which of the two options they intended.
              - When using the {!@actions.CreateSlackRecordChannel} action to create a Slack channel, if the Salesforce record ID is not provided or implied, ask for it.
              - When using the {!@actions.CreateSlackChannel} action to create a Slack channel, if the Slack Channel name is not provided or implied, ask for it. A Slack Team ID (or Workspace ID) has the following regular expression - "^T[A-Z0-9]{2,}". If a Team ID (or Workspace ID) isn't provided or it doesn't match the regular expression, use the {!@actions.ListSlackWorkspaces} action for a list of possible workspaces. If multiple workspaces are returned, provide the user with the choices available and ask the user to choose one. Instead, if there is only one workspace available, use that. Do not automatically infer the Slack Team ID (or Workspace ID) from the $PageContext.slack_team context variable if its value begins with an "E". If the user doesn't specify whether the channel should be public or private, default to public.
              - When another action requires a WorkspaceID and none have been provided, use the {!@actions.ListSlackWorkspaces} action to retrieve a list of Workspaces to present to the user.
              - When asked to add users to a Slack channel, use the {!@actions.AddUsersToSlackChannel} action to add users to the corresponding Slack channel. If the Slack Channel ID is not provided or implied, ask for it.
              - AddUsersToSlackChannel Action Input Parameters: The channelId parameter is the Slack Channel ID to add people to. A Slack Channel ID is represented as a string like C12345678. If a string like "<#C123456789>" is provided, extract a Slack Channel ID from it by removing the "<#" and ">" characters. For example, the Channel ID in "<#C123456789>" is C123456789. The userIds parameter is a comma separated list of Slack User IDs to add to the provided Slack Channel. A single Slack User ID is represented as a string like U987654321. If a string like <@U987654321> is provided extract a Slack User ID from it by removing the <@ and > characters. For example, the Slack User in <@U987654321> is U987654321. The input here needs to be a comma separated list of Slack User IDs like U12345678,U987654321,U781345729.
              - AddUsersToSlackChannel Action Output Parameters: The userIds output is a comma separated list of users who were added to the channel. A single Slack User ID should be represented as <@U12345678>. If a string like U123456789 is provided as output, add the <@ and > characters at the start and end of the string respectively. For example, the Slack User ID U123456789 is converted to <@U123456789>. A comma separated list of Slack User IDs will be provided to you. If applicable, apply the conversion to each Slack User ID in the comma separated string.
              - When asked to share a canvas with Slack Users and/or Slack Channels, use the {!@actions.ShareSlackCanvas} action to share accordingly. If the Slack Channel ID nor list of Slack User IDs are not provided or implied, ask for them.
              - ShareSlackCanvas Action Input Parameters: The canvasId parameter is the unique identifier of the existing canvas to share. A Slack Canvas ID is represented as a string like F017CC8EGRG. This is required to ensure that the correct canvas document is shared. The userIds parameter accepts a comma-separated list of Slack User IDs to share the provided Slack Canvas with. A single Slack User ID is represented as a string like U987654321. If a string like <@U987654321> is provided, extract the Slack User ID from it by removing the <@ and > characters. For example, the Slack User ID in <@U987654321> is U987654321. The input here needs to be a comma-separated list of Slack User IDs like U12345678,U987654321,U781345729. The channelIds parameter accepts a comma-separated list of Slack Channel IDs to share the provided Slack Canvas with. A single Slack Channel ID is represented as a string like C987654321. If a string like "<#C987654321>" is provided, extract the Slack Channel ID from it by removing the "<#" and ">" characters. For example, the Slack Channel ID in "<#C987654321>" is C987654321. The input here needs to be a comma-separated list of Slack Channel IDs like C12345678,C987654321,C781345729.
              - An agent can send messages in three ways. You can send a message to a channel, start a direct message between users or send a message to a specific user as the agent. When the user wants to notify or communicate with a large audience such as an entire channel, use the {!@actions.SendMessageToSlackChannel} action. When the user is looking to start a direct message (DM) with another Slack user or is looking to be introduced to another Slack User with the agent present in the conversation, use the {!@actions.SendSlackDirectMessage} action. When the user wants to send a message to a Slack User, or wants to notify or inform a specific Slack User of some activity, use the {!@actions.SendMessageAsAgent} action to send the user a message as an agent. If you are not sure of the user's intention or if the user's intention is ambiguous, present the user with these three messaging options along with a description of what they do and ask the user for their choice.
              - When asked to start a direct message (DM) with a Slack User or to get introduced to a Slack User, use the {!@actions.SendSlackDirectMessage} action. Users can send DMs to Slack users using Slack user IDs and Salesforce user IDs. If given a Salesforce user ID, use the {!@actions.GetSlackUser} action to find the corresponding Slack user ID.
              - SendSlackDirectMessage Action Message Input Parameter: The message parameter is plain text or markdown message to be sent to a user. Do not include HTML tags. You can format markdown lists as ordered or unordered, but DO NOT mix the 2 formats in your message input parameter. A string like <@U123456789> represents a User mention in Slack. You can extract a Slack User ID from a mention by removing the <@ and > characters. For example, the User ID in <@U123456789> is U123456789. A string like "<#C123456789>" represents a Channel mention in Slack. You can extract a Slack Channel ID from a mention by removing the "<#" and ">" characters. For example, the Channel ID in "<#C123456789>" is C123456789. When providing information to a user, if a Slack User ID is detected in the content being provided, convert that ID into a Slack User @mention. For example if there is a reference to a User in a string like 'U123456789', wrap that string into a string surrounded with '<@' and '>', for instance: '<@123456789>'. When providing information to a user, if a Slack Channel ID is detected in the content being provided, convert that ID into a Slack Channel @mention. For example if there is a reference to a User in a string like 'U123456789', wrap that string into a string surrounded with '<#' and '>', for instance: '<#C123456789>'. Text like "John Doe" (email: johndoe@example.com slack_user_id: U1234567) is a reference to a Slack user named John Doe with user ID U1234567. Text quoted by backticks should be sent to Slack verbatim, including the backticks. User references, including those within text quoted by single-quotes or double-quotes, should be resolved to Slack user ID references (for example, <@U1234567>). Channel references, including those within text quoted by single-quotes or double-quotes, should be resolved to Slack channel ID references (for example, <#C1234567>).
              - When asked to send a message to a Slack channel, use the {!@actions.SendMessageToSlackChannel} action to send the message. If the Slack Channel ID is not provided or implied, ask for it.
              - SendMessageToSlackChannel Action Input Parameters: The channelId parameter is the Slack Channel ID of the Slack Channel to send a message to. A Slack Channel ID is represented as a string like C12345678. If a string like "<#C123456789>" is provided, extract a Slack Channel ID from it by removing the "<#" and ">" characters. For example, the Channel ID in "<#C123456789>" is C123456789. The message parameter is plain text or markdown message to be sent to a user. Do not include HTML tags. You can format markdown lists as ordered or unordered, but DO NOT mix the 2 formats in your message input parameter. A string like <@U123456789> represents a User mention in Slack. You can extract a Slack User ID from a mention by removing the <@ and > characters. For example, the User ID in <@U123456789> is U123456789. A string like "<#C123456789>" represents a Channel mention in Slack. You can extract a Slack Channel ID from a mention by removing the "<#" and ">" characters. For example, the Channel ID in "<#C123456789>" is C123456789. When providing information to a user, if a Slack User ID is detected in the content being provided, convert that ID into a Slack User @mention. For example if there is a reference to a User in a string like 'U123456789', wrap that string into a string surrounded with '<@' and '>', for instance: '<@U123456789>'. When providing information to a user, if a Slack Channel ID is detected in the content being provided, convert that ID into a Slack Channel @mention. For example if there is a reference to a Channel in a string like 'C123456789', wrap that string into a string surrounded with '<#' and '>', for instance: '<#C123456789>'. Text like "John Doe" (email: johndoe@example.com slack_user_id: U1234567) is a reference to a Slack user named John Doe with user ID U1234567. Text quoted by backticks should be sent to Slack verbatim, including the backticks. User references, including those within text quoted by single-quotes or double-quotes, should be resolved to Slack user ID references (for example, <@U1234567>). Channel references, including those within text quoted by single-quotes or double-quotes, should be resolved to Slack channel ID references (for example, <#C1234567>).
              - When asked to inform, send a message or to notify a Slack User, use the {!@actions.SendMessageAsAgent} action. If the Slack User ID and message are not provided or implied, ask for them. If given a Salesforce User ID, use the {!@actions.GetSlackUser} action to find the corresponding Slack User ID.
              - SendMessageAsAgent Action Input Parameters: The userId parameter is the Slack User ID of the user to send the message to. A Slack User ID is represented as a string like U12345678. If a string like <@U12345678> is provided, extract a Slack User ID from it by removing the <@ and > characters. For example, the User ID in <@U12345678> is U12345678. The message parameter is plain text or markdown message to be sent to a user. Do not include HTML tags. You can format markdown lists as ordered or unordered, but DO NOT mix the 2 formats in your message input parameter. A string like <@U123456789> represents a User mention in Slack. You can extract a Slack User ID from a mention by removing the <@ and > characters. For example, the User ID in <@U123456789> is U123456789. A string like "<#C123456789>" represents a Channel mention in Slack. You can extract a Slack Channel ID from a mention by removing the "<#" and ">" characters. For example, the Channel ID in "<#C123456789>" is C123456789. When providing information to a user, if a Slack User ID is detected in the content being provided, convert that ID into a Slack User @mention. For example if there is a reference to a User in a string like 'U123456789', wrap that string into a string surrounded with '<@' and '>', for instance: '<@123456789>'. When providing information to a user, if a Slack Channel ID is detected in the content being provided, convert that ID into a Slack Channel @mention. For example if there is a reference to a User in a string like 'U123456789', wrap that string into a string surrounded with '<#' and '>', for instance: '<#C123456789>'. Text like "John Doe" (email: johndoe@example.com slack_user_id: U1234567) is a reference to a Slack user named John Doe with user ID U1234567. Text quoted by backticks should be sent to Slack verbatim, including the backticks. User references, including those within text quoted by single-quotes or double-quotes, should be resolved to Slack user ID references (for example, <@U1234567>). Channel references, including those within text quoted by single-quotes or double-quotes, should be resolved to Slack channel ID references (for example, <#C1234567>).
              - When asked to to Summarize a Slack Channel, use the {!@actions.SummarizeSlackChannel} action.
              - SummarizeSlackChannel Action Input Parameters: The channelId parameter is the Slack Channel ID the user will provide (e.g., C01ABC12345). If the channel provided comes in the format of '<#C0150UQ9MHR|>' where the channel Id is wrapped in '<# |>', remove the '|' to alter the channel Id reference. For example, '<#C1234ABC456|>' should be converted to '<#C1234ABC456>'. If the channel provided comes in the format of 'C1234ABC456' where the channel Id is a simple string wrap it with '<#C1234ABC456>' to alter the channel Id reference. For example, 'C1234ABC456' should be converted to '<#C0150UQ9MHR>'. The searchTimeRange parameter specifies the number of past calendar days to include in the summary. Do not accept negative numbers. The Maximum value accepted here is 30. If the user does not explicitly specify a value, default to 7. This determines how far back in time the Slack messages will be summarized, starting from today.
              - A "Canvas" or "Slack Canvas" is a file in Slack that contains plaintext or markdown. When a user references a "canvas", it should be considered in this context.
              - Canvas Content Formatting Instructions: When providing the 'content' input parameter for {!@actions.CreateSlackCanvas} or {!@actions.UpdateSlackCanvas}, format as markdown representation of canvas content. You can add sections, include links, references, and any other information you deem relevant. You can format markdown lists as ordered or unordered, but DO NOT mix the 2 formats in this input parameter.
              - Always convert content from Slack markdown to Standard markdown and apply these conversions for both user entered content and agent generated content: Bold: convert *bold* to **bold**. Italic: convert _italic_ to *italic*. Strikethrough: convert ~strike~ to ~~strike~~.
              - Canvas Headers: Never exceed Header depth of 3 (e.g. "###"). Truncate any Headers that exceed a depth of 3 to 3 (e.g. "####" convert to "###").
              - Canvas Lists: You can format markdown lists as ordered or unordered, but DO NOT mix the 2 formats in your content input parameter. Always maintain ordered and unordered lists. Whitespace: Always maintain spaces and newlines when possible.
              - Canvas User Mentions (CANVAS CONTENT PARAMETER ONLY - NOT RESPONSE MESSAGES): When formatting the 'content' input parameter for {!@actions.CreateSlackCanvas} or {!@actions.UpdateSlackCanvas}, if a Slack User is detected in the content being provided, convert that ID into Standard markdown for a Slack User at-mention. For example if there is a reference to a user in a string like '@U123456789' or '<@U123456789>', extract the ID and wrap it into a string surrounded with '![](@' and ')', for instance: User Id: U123456789 should always be converted to '![](@U123456789)'; User at-mention: '<@U123456789>' should always be converted to '![](@U123456789)'.
              - Canvas Channel Mentions (CANVAS CONTENT PARAMETER ONLY - NOT RESPONSE MESSAGES): When formatting the 'content' input parameter for {!@actions.CreateSlackCanvas} or {!@actions.UpdateSlackCanvas}, if a Slack Channel is detected in the content being provided, convert that ID into Standard markdown for a Slack Channel mention. For example if there is a reference to a channel in a string like '#C123456789', '<#C123456789>' or '<#C123456789|>', extract the ID and wrap it into a string surrounded with '![](#' and ')', for instance: Channel Id: 'C123456789' should always be converted to '![](#C123456789)'; Channel mention: '<#C123456789|>' OR '<#C123456789>' should always be converted to '![](#C123456789)'.
              - When asked to reply to a Slack message or a thread, use the {!@actions.ReplyInThread} action. If the Slack Channel ID is not provided or implied, ask for it. For message timestamp input, use the format <0123456789.012345>. If no message timestamp is provided or it is ambiguous in the session context, confirm which message the user intends to reply.
              - ReplyInThread Action Input Parameters: The recipientId parameter can contain either a Channel ID of the Slack Channel or a User Id to send a message to. A Slack Channel ID is represented as a string like C12345678 or D123456778. If a string like "<#C123456789>" or "<#D123456789>" is provided, extract a Slack Channel ID from it by removing the "<#" and ">" characters. A Slack User ID is represented as a string like U12345678. If a string like <@U123456789> is provided, extract a Slack User ID from it by removing the <@ and > characters. For example, the Channel ID in <@U123456789> is U123456789. The messageText parameter is plain text or markdown message to be sent to a user. Do not include HTML tags. You can format markdown lists as ordered or unordered, but DO NOT mix the 2 formats in your message input parameter. A string like <@U123456789> represents a User mention in Slack. You can extract a Slack User ID from a mention by removing the <@ and > characters. For example, the User ID in <@U123456789> is U123456789. A string like "<#C123456789>" represents a Channel mention in Slack. You can extract a Slack Channel ID from a mention by removing the "<#" and ">" characters. For example, the Channel ID in "<#C123456789>" is C123456789. When providing information to a user, if a Slack User ID is detected in the content being provided, convert that ID into a Slack User @mention. For example if there is a reference to a User in a string like 'U123456789', wrap that string into a string surrounded with '<@' and '>', for instance: '<@U123456789>'. When providing information to a user, if a Slack Channel ID is detected in the content being provided, convert that ID into a Slack Channel @mention. For example if there is a reference to a Channel in a string like 'C123456789', wrap that string into a string surrounded with '<#' and '>', for instance: '<#C123456789>'. Text like "John Doe" (email: johndoe@example.com slack_user_id: U1234567) is a reference to a Slack user named John Doe with user ID U1234567. Text quoted by backticks should be sent to Slack verbatim, including the backticks. User references, including those within text quoted by single-quotes or double-quotes, should be resolved to Slack user ID references (for example, <@U1234567>). Channel references, including those within text quoted by single-quotes or double-quotes, should be resolved to Slack channel ID references (for example, <#C1234567>). The messageTs parameter is the message timestamp of the parent slack message. A message timestamp is represented as a string like 0123456789.012345 (E.g 1752656148.567749).
              - Upon successful completion of {!@actions.CreateSlackCanvas}, {!@actions.UpdateSlackCanvas}, {!@actions.ShareSlackCanvas}, {!@actions.CreateSlackRecordChannel}, {!@actions.CreateSlackChannel}, {!@actions.SendSlackDirectMessage}, {!@actions.SendMessageToSlackChannel}, or {!@actions.SendMessageAsAgent}, provide the user a friendly confirmation with the URL link formatted as markdown hyperlinks using the syntax [link text](url). When mentioning users or channels in your confirmation message, use native Slack mention format: <@userId> for users and <#channelId> for channels. Do NOT use the canvas markdown format (![](#) or ![](@)) in response messages.
        actions:
            CreateSlackCanvas: @actions.CreateSlackCanvas
                with title=...
                with content=...
            UpdateSlackCanvas: @actions.UpdateSlackCanvas
                with canvasId=...
                with content=...
            GetSlackUser: @actions.GetSlackUser
                with salesforceUserId=...
            SearchSlack: @actions.SearchSlack
                with query=...
                with contentTypes=...
                with channelTypes=...
                with contextChannelId=...
                with includeChannels=...
                with excludeChannels=...
            SendSlackDirectMessage: @actions.SendSlackDirectMessage
                with slackUserId=...
                with message=...
            LookupSlackRecordChannel: @actions.LookupSlackRecordChannel
                with recordId=...
            CreateSlackRecordChannel: @actions.CreateSlackRecordChannel
                with recordId=...
            CreateSlackChannel: @actions.CreateSlackChannel
                with channelName=...
                with teamId=...
                with isPrivate=...
            ListSlackWorkspaces: @actions.ListSlackWorkspaces
                with emptyInput=...
            ArchiveSlackChannel: @actions.ArchiveSlackChannel
                with channelId=...
            AddUsersToSlackChannel: @actions.AddUsersToSlackChannel
                with channelId=...
                with userIds=...
            ShareSlackCanvas: @actions.ShareSlackCanvas
                with canvasId=...
                with userIds=...
                with channelIds=...
                with accessLevel=...
            SendMessageToSlackChannel: @actions.SendMessageToSlackChannel
                with channelId=...
                with message=...
            SendMessageAsAgent: @actions.SendMessageAsAgent
                with userId=...
                with message=...
                with recommendedActions=...
                with aiGenActionItemIdInContextInput = ...
            SummarizeSlackChannel: @actions.SummarizeSlackChannel
                with channelId=...
                with searchTimeRange=...
                with searchFilterTerms=...
                with summaryTemplateName=...
            ReplyInThread: @actions.ReplyInThread
                with recipientId=...
                with messageText=...
                with messageTs=...
    actions:
        CreateSlackCanvas:
            description: "Create a Slack canvas document with the provided markdown content.\nYou can add sections, include links, references, and any other information you deem relevant.\nWhen asked to create a canvas with prior content, ask the user whether there is a desired outline with sections, formatting, and sequencing preferred before creating the canvas.\nUpon successful completion, provide the user a friendly confirmation including the canvas link in markdown.\n"
            label: "Create a Slack Canvas"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Creating Slack canvas..."
            source: "Slack__CreateSlackCanvas"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://slackAgentCreateCanvas"
            inputs:
                "title": string
                    description: "{!$Label.CreateSlackCanvasAction.TitleInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.CreateSlackCanvasAction.TitleInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "content": string
                    description: "{!$Label.CreateSlackCanvasAction.ContentInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.CreateSlackCanvasAction.ContentInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
            outputs:
                "canvasId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.CreateSlackCanvasAction.CanvasIdOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.CreateSlackCanvasAction.CanvasIdOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
                "canvasUrl": string
                    description: "{!$Label.CreateSlackCanvasAction.CanvasUrlOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.CreateSlackCanvasAction.CanvasUrlOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        UpdateSlackCanvas:
            description: "Append markdown content to a Slack canvas document.\nAlways append new content and never duplicate content that was added in earlier prompts.\nIf no canvas ID is provided or it is ambiguous in the session context, confirm which canvas ID the user intends to update.\nUpon successful completion, provide the user a friendly confirmation with a link to the canvas (in markdown).\n"
            label: "Update a Slack Canvas"
            require_user_confirmation: True
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Updating Slack canvas..."
            source: "Slack__UpdateSlackCanvas"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://slackAgentUpdateCanvas"
            inputs:
                "canvasId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.UpdateSlackCanvasAction.CanvasIdInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.UpdateSlackCanvasAction.CanvasIdInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: False
                "content": string
                    description: "{!$Label.UpdateSlackCanvasAction.ContentInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.UpdateSlackCanvasAction.ContentInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
            outputs:
                "canvasId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.UpdateSlackCanvasAction.CanvasIdOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.UpdateSlackCanvasAction.CanvasIdOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
                "canvasUrl": string
                    description: "{!$Label.UpdateSlackCanvasAction.CanvasUrlOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.UpdateSlackCanvasAction.CanvasUrlOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        GetSlackUser:
            description: "Given a Salesforce user ID, looks up the corresponding Slack user ID."
            label: "Look Up a Slack User"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Looking Up a Slack user..."
            source: "Slack__GetSlackUser"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://slackAgentGetUser"
            inputs:
                salesforceUserId: object
                    description: "{!$Label.GetSlackUserAction.SalesforceUserIdInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.GetSlackUserAction.SalesforceUserIdInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__recordIdType"
            outputs:
                slackUserId: string
                    description: "{!$Label.GetSlackUserAction.SlackUserIdOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.GetSlackUserAction.SlackUserIdOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
        SearchSlack:
            description: "Performs search on Slack\nSearch query input accepts the following forms:\n - keywords (e.g. 'notes')\n - phrases (e.g. 'meeting notes')\n - questions (e.g. 'Where are the meeting notes for the sync meeting yesterday?')\nWhen appropriate, (e.g. The user asked a specific question), use the 'question' option for the query input by passing the original raw question from the user.\nReturns three types of objects:\n * \"messages\": Slack messages found in Slack channels and are accessible to the acting user\n * \"files\": Files found in Slack of all types that are accessible to the acting user\n * \"enterprise\": Search result objects from various third party systems that are connected and authenticated by the acting user. Each enterprise object returned will include a 'lookup_function' object which will provide details of what third party system and instance the data was retrieved from with some contextual information about the data. Use that information to organize and process all of the contents in each object.\n All three object types should be used to provide the user with a comprehensive summary by evaluating and considering the context of each object to best answer the user's query.\n\nClarifications and Refinements: If the query is vague, ask clarifying questions. If search results are insufficient or outdated, suggest next steps.\nDo not use any data or information outside of Slack's knowledge base. The agent should only retrieve and provide information that is available within the Slack workspace and should not pull from external sources\n\nFormatting Search Results:\n * A string like <@U123456789> or <@W123456789> represents a User mention in Slack. You can extract a Slack User ID from a mention by removing the <@ and > characters. For example, the User ID in <@U123456789> is U123456789.\n * A string like <#C123456789> or <#D123456789> represents a Channel mention in Slack. You can extract a Slack Channel ID from a mention by removing the <# and > characters. For example, the Channel ID in <#C123456789> is C123456789.\n * When providing information to a user, if a Slack User ID is detected in the content being provided, convert that ID into a Slack User at-mention. For example if there is a reference to a user in a string like 'U123456789' or 'W123456789', wrap that string into a string surrounded with  '<@' and  '>', for instance: <@U123456789>.\n * When providing information to a user, if a Slack Channel ID is detected in the content being provided, convert that ID into a Slack Channel mention. For example if there is a reference to a channel in a string like 'C123456789' or 'D123456789', wrap that string into a string surrounded with  '<#' and  '>', for instance: <#C123456789>.\n\nProcessing Search Results:\n * Retrieve and analyze search results.\n * Summarize relevant responses clearly and concisely.\n * If multiple relevant messages exist, synthesize the information into a coherent answer.\n * If no useful results are found, acknowledge the lack of results and suggest rephrasing the query or asking in relevant Slack channels.\n * Do not list the individual messages or their content. Instead, identify recurring themes, keywords, or subjects.\n Example:\n   * User Prompt: 'Find messages about project deadlines.';\n   * Response: 'The messages discuss topics such as project timelines, task assignments, and upcoming deliverables.'\n\nGeneral Questions: For general questions, provide summaries as usual. Process the messages.matches array to identify recurring themes, topics, or significant details.\n\nError or No Data Scenarios:\n * If the search query returns no matching messages, respond appropriately: 'No messages were found matching your search criteria. Please refine your query and try again.'\n"
            label: "Search Slack"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Searching Slack..."
            source: "Slack__SearchSlack"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://slackAgentSearch"
            inputs:
                query: string
                    description: "{!$Label.SearchSlackAction.QueryInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SearchSlackAction.QueryInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                contentTypes: string
                    description: "{!$Label.SearchSlackAction.ContentTypesInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SearchSlackAction.ContentTypesInputTitle}"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                channelTypes: string
                    description: "{!$Label.SearchSlackAction.ChannelTypesInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SearchSlackAction.ChannelTypesInputTitle}"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                contextChannelId: string
                    description: "{!$Label.SearchSlackAction.ContextChannelIdInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SearchSlackAction.ContextChannelIdInputTitle}"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: False
                includeChannels: string
                    description: "Comma separated list of channel IDs to specifically include in the search results. When provided, the search will only return results from these specified channels. Channel IDs should be in the format 'C1234567890'. This parameter works in conjunction with other search filters."
                    label: "Include channels"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                excludeChannels: string
                    description: "Comma separated list of channel IDs to exclude from the search results. When provided, the search will filter out any results from these specified channels. Channel IDs should be in the format 'C1234567890'. This parameter works in conjunction with other search filters."
                    label: "Exclude channels"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
            outputs:
                results: string
                    description: "{!$Label.SearchSlackAction.ResultsOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SearchSlackAction.ResultsOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        SendSlackDirectMessage:
            description: "Given plain text or markdown text, send a direct message (DM) in Slack with the recipient and sender users in the DM channel.\nYou can add sections, include links, references, and any other information you deem relevant.\nProvide the message url to the user along with a friendly message.\nUpon successful completion, provide the user a friendly confirmation with a link to the message (in markdown).\n"
            label: "Send a Slack Direct Message"
            require_user_confirmation: True
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Sending Slack direct message..."
            source: "Slack__SendSlackDirectMessage"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://slackAgentSendDirectMessage"
            inputs:
                slackUserId: string
                    description: "{!$Label.SendSlackDirectMessageAction.SlackUserIdInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SendSlackDirectMessageAction.SlackUserIdInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                message: string
                    description: "{!$Label.SendSlackDirectMessageAction.MessageInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SendSlackDirectMessageAction.MessageInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
            outputs:
                channelId: string
                    description: "{!$Label.SendSlackDirectMessageAction.ChannelIdOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SendSlackDirectMessageAction.ChannelIdOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
                messageUrl: string
                    description: "{!$Label.SendSlackDirectMessageAction.MessageUrlOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SendSlackDirectMessageAction.MessageUrlOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
                messageTs: string
                    description: "{!$Label.SendSlackDirectMessageAction.MessageTsOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SendSlackDirectMessageAction.MessageTsOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        LookupSlackRecordChannel:
            description: "Given a Salesforce record ID, looks up the corresponding record channel in Slack.\nUpon successful completion, provide the channel at-mention and url to the user along with a friendly message.\n"
            label: "Look Up a Salesforce Channel in Slack"
            require_user_confirmation: True
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Looking up a Salesforce Channel in Slack..."
            source: "Slack__LookupSlackRecordChannel"
            target: "slack://slackAgentDynamic__LookupSlackRecordChannel"
            inputs:
                "recordId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.LookupSlackRecordChannelAction.RecordIdInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.LookupSlackRecordChannelAction.RecordIdInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
            outputs:
                "channelId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.LookupSlackRecordChannelAction.ChannelIdOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.LookupSlackRecordChannelAction.ChannelIdOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: True
                "channelUrl": string
                    description: "{!$Label.LookupSlackRecordChannelAction.ChannelUrlOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.LookupSlackRecordChannelAction.ChannelUrlOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        CreateSlackRecordChannel:
            description: "Given a Salesforce record ID, creates a corresponding record channel in Slack. Provide the channel at-mention and url to the user along with a friendly message."
            label: "Create a Salesforce Channel in Slack"
            require_user_confirmation: True
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Creating a Slack channel..."
            source: "Slack__CreateSlackRecordChannel"
            target: "slack://slackAgentDynamic__CreateSlackRecordChannel"
            inputs:
                "recordId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.CreateSlackRecordChannelAction.RecordIdInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.CreateSlackRecordChannelAction.RecordIdInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
            outputs:
                "channelId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.CreateSlackRecordChannelAction.ChannelIdOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.CreateSlackRecordChannelAction.ChannelIdOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
                "channelUrl": string
                    description: "{!$Label.CreateSlackRecordChannelAction.ChannelUrlOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.CreateSlackRecordChannelAction.ChannelUrlOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
        CreateSlackChannel:
            description: "Create a Slack Channel.\nAsk the end user for a Channel name, the Team ID (or Workspace ID) to create the Slack Channel in and whether the Channel is public or private, unless these details are already provided.\nUpon successful completion, provide the channel at-mention and url to the user along with a friendly message.\n"
            label: "Create a Slack Channel"
            require_user_confirmation: True
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Creating a Slack channel..."
            source: "Slack__CreateSlackChannel"
            target: "slack://slackAgentDynamic__CreateChannel"
            inputs:
                "channelName": string
                    description: "{!$Label.CreateSlackChannelAction.ChannelNameInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.CreateSlackChannelAction.ChannelNameInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "teamId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.CreateSlackChannelAction.TeamIdInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.CreateSlackChannelAction.TeamIdInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "isPrivate": boolean
                    description: "{!$Label.CreateSlackChannelAction.IsPrivateInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.CreateSlackChannelAction.IsPrivateInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
            outputs:
                "channelId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.CreateSlackChannelAction.ChannelIdOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.CreateSlackChannelAction.ChannelIdOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
                "channelUrl": string
                    description: "{!$Label.CreateSlackChannelAction.ChannelUrlOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.CreateSlackChannelAction.ChannelUrlOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        ListSlackWorkspaces:
            description: "List Workspaces in Slack.\n"
            label: "List Slack Workspaces"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Listing Slack workspaces..."
            source: "Slack__ListSlackWorkspaces"
            target: "slack://slackAgentDynamic__ListWorkspaces"
            inputs:
                "emptyInput": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ListSlackWorkspacesAction.EmptyInputInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ListSlackWorkspacesAction.EmptyInputInputTitle}"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: False
            outputs:
                "workspaces": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ListSlackWorkspacesAction.WorkspacesOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ListSlackWorkspacesAction.WorkspacesOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        ArchiveSlackChannel:
            description: "Archives a Slack Channel, given a Slack Channel ID. When asked to archive a Slack channel, ask for a Slack Channel ID unless already provided.\nUpon successful completion, provide the user a friendly confirmation with the channel at-mention and url.\n"
            label: "Archive a Slack Channel"
            require_user_confirmation: True
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Archiving a Slack channel..."
            source: "Slack__ArchiveSlackChannel"
            target: "slack://slackAgentDynamic__ArchiveSlackChannel"
            inputs:
                "channelId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ArchiveSlackChannelAction.ChannelIdInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ArchiveSlackChannelAction.ChannelIdInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
            outputs:
                "channelId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ArchiveSlackChannelAction.ChannelIdOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ArchiveSlackChannelAction.ChannelIdOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        AddUsersToSlackChannel:
            description: "Add Slack Users to a Slack Channel.\nIf a list of Slack Users to add to the channel is not provided, ask the user for the list of Slack users to add to the Slack channel.\nIf a Slack channel ID is not provided, ask the user for it.\nSlack User IDs can be provided as a comma separated string.\nUpon successful completion, provide the list of Slack User at-mentions and the Channel at-mention to the user along with a friendly message.\n"
            label: "Add Users or Agents to a Slack Channel"
            require_user_confirmation: True
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Adding users to a Slack channel..."
            source: "Slack__AddUsersToSlackChannel"
            target: "slack://slackAgentDynamic__AddUsersToSlackChannel"
            inputs:
                "channelId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.AddUsersToSlackChannelAction.ChannelIdInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.AddUsersToSlackChannelAction.ChannelIdInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "userIds": string
                    description: "{!$Label.AddUsersToSlackChannelAction.UserIdsInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.AddUsersToSlackChannelAction.UserIdsInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
            outputs:
                "userIds": string
                    description: "{!$Label.AddUsersToSlackChannelAction.UserIdsOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.AddUsersToSlackChannelAction.UserIdsOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        ShareSlackCanvas:
            description: "Shares a Slack Canvas with a set of users and/or channels.\nIf neither a list of Slack Users nor Slack Channels to to add to the channel is provided, ask the user for a list of Slack Users and/or Slack Channels to share the Canvas with.\nIf the user does not provide an access level for the shared Canvas, ask the user for it.\nUpon successful completion, provide the user a friendly confirmation with a link to the canvas (in markdown) and at-mentions for the channels and/or Users the Canvas was shared with.\n"
            label: "Share a Slack Canvas"
            require_user_confirmation: True
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Sharing a Slack canvas..."
            source: "Slack__ShareSlackCanvas"
            target: "slack://slackAgentDynamic__ShareSlackCanvas"
            inputs:
                "canvasId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.CanvasIdInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.CanvasIdInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "userIds": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.UserIdsInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.UserIdsInputTitle}"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                "channelIds": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.ChannelIdsInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.ChannelIdsInputTitle}"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                "accessLevel": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.AccessLevelInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.AccessLevelInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
            outputs:
                "canvasId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.CanvasIdOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.CanvasIdOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
                "canvasUrl": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.CanvasUrlOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.CanvasUrlOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        SendMessageToSlackChannel:
            description: "Sends a message to a public or private Slack Channel.\nMessages may be in plaintext or Markdown format.\nThis action is intended for group communication, announcements, or notifications within channels.\nThis action should not be used to send direct messages to individuals.\nUpon successful completion, provide the user a friendly confirmation with a link to the message (in markdown).\n"
            label: "Send Message to a Slack Channel"
            require_user_confirmation: True
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Sending message..."
            source: "Slack__SendMessageToSlackChannel"
            target: "slack://slackAgentDynamic__SendMessageToSlackChannel"
            inputs:
                "channelId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.SendMessageToSlackChannelAction.ChannelIdInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SendMessageToSlackChannelAction.ChannelIdInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "message": string
                    description: "{!$Label.SendMessageToSlackChannelAction.MessageInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SendMessageToSlackChannelAction.MessageInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
            outputs:
                "messageUrl": string
                    description: "{!$Label.SendMessageToSlackChannelAction.MessageUrlOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SendMessageToSlackChannelAction.MessageUrlOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
                "messageTs": string
                    description: "{!$Label.SendMessageToSlackChannelAction.MessageTsOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SendMessageToSlackChannelAction.MessageTsOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        SendMessageAsAgent:
            description: "Use to send notifications or messages to specific Slack users in a direct message from the agent.\nMessages may be sent in plain text or formatted using Markdown.\nThis action is intended to send notifications, inform or message specific Slack Users.\nThis action cannot be used to send messages to channels.\nUpon successful completion, provide the user a friendly confirmation with a link to the message (in markdown).\n"
            label: "Start a Slack conversation with an Agent"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Starting a Slack conversation with an Agent..."
            source: "Slack__SendMessageAsAgent"
            target: "slack://slackAgentDynamic__SendMessageAsAgent"
            inputs:
                "userId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.SendMessageAsAgentAction.UserIdInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SendMessageAsAgentAction.UserIdInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "message": string
                    description: "{!$Label.SendMessageAsAgentAction.MessageInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SendMessageAsAgentAction.MessageInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "recommendedActions": list[object]
                    description: "{!$Label.SendMessageAsAgentAction.RecommendedActionsInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SendMessageAsAgentAction.RecommendedActionsInputTitle}"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                    complex_data_type_name: "slack_invocable_actions__promptActionButton"
                "aiGenActionItemIdInContextInput": string
                    description: "{!$Label.SendMessageAsAgentAction.AiGenActionItemIdInContextInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SendMessageAsAgentAction.AiGenActionItemIdInContextInputTitle}"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: False
            outputs:
                "messageUrl": string
                    description: "{!$Label.SendMessageAsAgentAction.MessageUrlOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SendMessageAsAgentAction.MessageUrlOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
                "messageTs": string
                    description: "{!$Label.SendMessageAsAgentAction.MessageTsOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SendMessageAsAgentAction.MessageTsOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        SummarizeSlackChannel:
            description: "Uses the Slack Search API to find relevant messages, files, and sources in a channel during a specified timeframe. Then, uses the search results in a prompt template to summarize results in a readable format."
            label: "Summarize a Slack Channel"
            require_user_confirmation: True
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Summarizing a Slack channel..."
            source: "Slack__SummarizeSlackChannel"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://slackAgentSummarizeChannel"
            inputs:
                "channelId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.SummarizeSlackChannelAction.ChannelIdInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SummarizeSlackChannelAction.ChannelIdInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "searchTimeRange": object
                    description: "{!$Label.SummarizeSlackChannelAction.SearchTimeRangeInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SummarizeSlackChannelAction.SearchTimeRangeInputTitle}"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__integerType"
                "searchFilterTerms": string
                    description: "{!$Label.SummarizeSlackChannelAction.SearchFilterTermsInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SummarizeSlackChannelAction.SearchFilterTermsInputTitle}"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                "summaryTemplateName": string
                    description: "{!$Label.SummarizeSlackChannelAction.SummaryTemplateNameInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SummarizeSlackChannelAction.SummaryTemplateNameInputTitle}"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
            outputs:
                "channelSummary": object
                    description: "{!$Label.SummarizeSlackChannelAction.ChannelSummaryOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.SummarizeSlackChannelAction.ChannelSummaryOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__richTextType"
        ReplyInThread:
            description: "Replies with a message in thread in a Slack channel or direct message. Messages may be in plain text or Markdown format. If no message timestamp is provided or it is ambiguous in the session context, confirm which message the user intends to reply. Upon successful completion, provide the user a friendly confirmation with a link to the message, formatted using Markdown.\n"
            label: "Reply to a Slack thread"
            require_user_confirmation: True
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Replying to a thread..."
            source: "Slack__ReplyInThread"
            target: "slack://slackAgentDynamic__ReplyInThread"
            inputs:
                "recipientId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ReplyInThreadSlackAction.RecipientIdInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ReplyInThreadSlackAction.RecipientIdInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "messageText": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ReplyInThreadSlackAction.MessageTextInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ReplyInThreadSlackAction.MessageTextInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "messageTs": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ReplyInThreadSlackAction.MessageTsInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ReplyInThreadSlackAction.MessageTsInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
            outputs:
                "messageUrl": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ReplyInThreadSlackAction.MessageUrlOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ReplyInThreadSlackAction.MessageUrlOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
                "messageTs": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ReplyInThreadSlackAction.MessageTsOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ReplyInThreadSlackAction.MessageTsOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False

subagent SlackExecutiveBrief:
    label: "Slack Executive Brief"
    description: "Allows agents to use a Salesforce prompt template to create executive brief canvases in Slack."
    reasoning:
        instructions: ->
            | Your job is to help create an executive brief for a Salesforce record in Slack by creating, updating and sharing a Slack canvas.
              Additional instructions follow:
              - When an action results in an error, summarize the error message with a user friendly reason so that the user can take appropriate action.
              - When asked to create a canvas, use the {!@actions.CreateSlackCanvas} action.
              - When asked to update, append to, or add content to a canvas, use the {!@actions.UpdateSlackCanvas} action. Always append new content and never duplicate content that was added in earlier prompts. If no canvas ID is provided or it is ambiguous in the session context, confirm which canvas ID the user intends to update.
              - Canvas Content Formatting Instructions: When providing the 'content' input parameter for {!@actions.CreateSlackCanvas} or {!@actions.UpdateSlackCanvas}, format as markdown representation of canvas content. You can add sections, include links, references, and any other information you deem relevant. You can format markdown lists as ordered or unordered, but DO NOT mix the 2 formats in this input parameter.
              - When asked to share a canvas with Slack Users and/or Slack Channels, use the {!@actions.ShareSlackCanvas} action to share accordingly. If the Slack Channel ID nor list of Slack User IDs are not provided or implied, ask for them.
              - ShareSlackCanvas Action Input Parameters: The canvasId parameter is the unique identifier of the existing canvas to share. A Slack Canvas ID is represented as a string like F017CC8EGRG. This is required to ensure that the correct canvas document is shared. The userIds parameter accepts a comma-separated list of Slack User IDs to share the provided Slack Canvas with. A single Slack User ID is represented as a string like U987654321. If a string like <@U987654321> is provided, extract the Slack User ID from it by removing the <@ and > characters. For example, the Slack User ID in <@U987654321> is U987654321. The input here needs to be a comma-separated list of Slack User IDs like U12345678,U987654321,U781345729. The channelIds parameter accepts a comma-separated list of Slack Channel IDs to share the provided Slack Canvas with. A single Slack Channel ID is represented as a string like C987654321. If a string like "<#C987654321>" is provided, extract the Slack Channel ID from it by removing the "<#" and ">" characters. For example, the Slack Channel ID in "<#C987654321>" is C987654321. The input here needs to be a comma-separated list of Slack Channel IDs like C12345678,C987654321,C781345729.
              - Use the {!@actions.IdentifyRecordByName} action to identify a record by name. When a record name is not provided, ask the user for it.
              - Use the {!@actions.GetRecordDetails} action to get record details for a record. When a record ID is not provided, ask the user for it. Alternatively, if a record name is provided, the record ID can be obtained by using the output of the {!@actions.IdentifyRecordByName} action.
              - When asked to create an executive brief for an account, use the {!@actions.ExecutiveBrief} action to get a summary of the executive brief. Pass this information in to {!@actions.CreateSlackCanvas} to create a Slack Canvas with the account's executive brief. Ensure that the Slack Canvas is created accurately based on the prompt template. Share the link to the Slack Canvas with the user.
              - If a user requests to search an account, use {!@actions.IdentifyRecordByName} to search for the account
              - If the account cannot be found, ask the user for more details
              - Upon successful completion of {!@actions.CreateSlackCanvas}, {!@actions.UpdateSlackCanvas}, or {!@actions.ShareSlackCanvas}, provide the user a friendly confirmation with the URL link formatted as markdown hyperlinks using the syntax [link text](url). When mentioning users or channels in your confirmation message, use native Slack mention format: <@userId> for users and <#channelId> for channels. Do NOT use the canvas markdown format (![](#) or ![](@)) in response messages.
        actions:
            CreateSlackCanvas: @actions.CreateSlackCanvas
                with title=...
                with content=...
            UpdateSlackCanvas: @actions.UpdateSlackCanvas
                with canvasId=...
                with content=...
            ShareSlackCanvas: @actions.ShareSlackCanvas
                with canvasId=...
                with userIds=...
                with channelIds=...
                with accessLevel=...
            ExecutiveBrief: @actions.ExecutiveBrief
                with "Input:Account"=...
            IdentifyRecordByName: @actions.IdentifyRecordByName
                with recordName=...
                with objectApiName=...
            GetRecordDetails: @actions.GetRecordDetails
                with recordId=...
    actions:
        CreateSlackCanvas:
            description: "Create a Slack canvas document with the provided markdown content.\nYou can add sections, include links, references, and any other information you deem relevant.\nWhen asked to create a canvas with prior content, ask the user whether there is a desired outline with sections, formatting, and sequencing preferred before creating the canvas.\nUpon successful completion, provide the user a friendly confirmation including the canvas link in markdown.\n"
            label: "Create a Slack Canvas"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Creating Slack canvas..."
            source: "Slack__CreateSlackCanvas"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://slackAgentCreateCanvas"
            inputs:
                "title": string
                    description: "{!$Label.CreateSlackCanvasAction.TitleInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.CreateSlackCanvasAction.TitleInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "content": string
                    description: "{!$Label.CreateSlackCanvasAction.ContentInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.CreateSlackCanvasAction.ContentInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
            outputs:
                "canvasId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.CreateSlackCanvasAction.CanvasIdOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.CreateSlackCanvasAction.CanvasIdOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
                "canvasUrl": string
                    description: "{!$Label.CreateSlackCanvasAction.CanvasUrlOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.CreateSlackCanvasAction.CanvasUrlOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        UpdateSlackCanvas:
            description: "Append markdown content to a Slack canvas document.\nAlways append new content and never duplicate content that was added in earlier prompts.\nIf no canvas ID is provided or it is ambiguous in the session context, confirm which canvas ID the user intends to update.\nUpon successful completion, provide the user a friendly confirmation with a link to the canvas (in markdown).\n"
            label: "Update a Slack Canvas"
            require_user_confirmation: True
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Updating Slack canvas..."
            source: "Slack__UpdateSlackCanvas"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://slackAgentUpdateCanvas"
            inputs:
                "canvasId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.UpdateSlackCanvasAction.CanvasIdInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.UpdateSlackCanvasAction.CanvasIdInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: False
                "content": string
                    description: "{!$Label.UpdateSlackCanvasAction.ContentInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.UpdateSlackCanvasAction.ContentInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
            outputs:
                "canvasId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.UpdateSlackCanvasAction.CanvasIdOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.UpdateSlackCanvasAction.CanvasIdOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
                "canvasUrl": string
                    description: "The Slack canvas URL for the updated canvas."
                    label: "{!$Label.UpdateSlackCanvasAction.CanvasUrlOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        ShareSlackCanvas:
            description: "Shares a Slack Canvas with a set of users and/or channels.\nIf neither a list of Slack Users nor Slack Channels to to add to the channel is provided, ask the user for a list of Slack Users and/or Slack Channels to share the Canvas with.\nIf the user does not provide an access level for the shared Canvas, ask the user for it.\nUpon successful completion, provide the user a friendly confirmation with a link to the canvas (in markdown) and at-mentions for the channels and/or Users the Canvas was shared with.\n"
            label: "Share a Slack Canvas"
            require_user_confirmation: True
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Sharing a Slack canvas..."
            source: "Slack__ShareSlackCanvas"
            target: "slack://slackAgentDynamic__ShareSlackCanvas"
            inputs:
                "canvasId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.CanvasIdInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.CanvasIdInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "userIds": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.UserIdsInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.UserIdsInputTitle}"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                "channelIds": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.ChannelIdsInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.ChannelIdsInputTitle}"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                "accessLevel": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.AccessLevelInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.AccessLevelInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
            outputs:
                "canvasId": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.CanvasIdOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.CanvasIdOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
                "canvasUrl": string
                    description: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.CanvasUrlOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ShareSlackCanvasAction.CanvasUrlOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        ExecutiveBrief:
            description: "Given an Account record, generate an executive brief of that account grounded with details present in the account object using a prompt template"
            label: "Create an Account Executive Brief"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Creating the executive brief..."
            source: "Slack__ExecutiveBrief"
            target: "generatePromptResponse://Slack__ExecutiveBriefPromptTemplate"
            inputs:
                "Input:Account": object
                    description: "{!$Label.ExecutiveBriefAction.Input:AccountInputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ExecutiveBriefAction.Input:AccountInputTitle}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__recordInfoType"
            outputs:
                "promptResponse": object
                    description: "{!$Label.ExecutiveBriefAction.PromptResponseOutputDescription}"
                    label: "{!$Label.ExecutiveBriefAction.PromptResponseOutputTitle}"
                    is_displayable: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__richTextType"
        IdentifyRecordByName:
            description: "Searches for Salesforce CRM records by name and returns a list of matching Salesforce CRM record IDs."
            label: "Identify Record by Name"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            source: "EmployeeCopilot__IdentifyRecordByName"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://identifyRecordByName"
            inputs:
                "recordName": string
                    description: "The name or title of the Salesforce record extracted from user input. The name can be used to find a Salesforce CRM record."
                    label: "recordName"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "objectApiName": string
                    description: "The API name of the Salesforce object (such as Account or Opportunity) associated with the record the user wants to find. The name can be obtained from the context and does not always require the identifyObjectByName action. (eg. IdentifyRecordByName(recordName=\"Paul\", objectApiName=\"user\")). Leave empty to check with all possible objectApiNames. Only use objectApiName field if a particular objectApiName type has been identified for this record in earlier step, otherwise leave empty to increase recall and query all objectApiNames by default (eg. IdentifyRecordByName(recordName=\"Paul\"))."
                    label: "objectApiName"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: False
            outputs:
                "searchResults": list[object]
                    description: "A list of the matching Salesforce record ids in descending order of relevance."
                    label: "searchResults"
                    is_displayable: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__recordInfoType"
        GetRecordDetails:
            description: "Generates a text blob containing record details, including object fields and values and records from related lists."
            label: "Get Record Details"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Getting details"
            source: "EmployeeCopilot__GetRecordDetails"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://getDataForGrounding"
            inputs:
                "recordId": object
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetRecordDetails.InvocableActionInputRecordIdDesc}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetRecordDetails.InvocableActionInputRecordIdLabel}"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__recordIdType"
            outputs:
                "snapshot": string
                    description: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetRecordDetails.InvocableActionRecordDetailsOutputDesc}"
                    label: "{!$Label.InvocableActionGetRecordDetails.InvocableActionRecordDetailsOutputLabel}"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False

subagent operaciones:
    label: "Operaciones"
    description: "Responde preguntas de operación y estrategia del trimestre de Changarro: avance contra la meta por región, causas raíz de retrasos cruzando ERP, Jira y soporte, escalación de clientes bloqueados y búsqueda de prospectos reales en INEGI DENUE."
    reasoning:
        instructions: ->
            | AVANCE: para "¿vamos bien?", "¿cómo va el trimestre?" o una región, usa {!@actions.GetQuarterHealth}. Deja region vacía si no la mencionan. Resume primero la región en riesgo y luego las demás en una línea cada una.
            | POR QUÉ: para "¿por qué la Península?", "¿qué está bloqueando?" o "¿qué clientes están en riesgo?", usa {!@actions.GetRegionRisk} con la región. Destaca la causa raíz compartida, cuántos clientes y cuánto dinero, cuántos tienen casos abiertos, y cuánto subiría la región si se resuelve. Lista los clientes de forma compacta.
            | ESCALAR, PASO 1: cuando pidan escalar, usa {!@actions.EscalateBlockedCustomers} con la región, la clave de Jira de la causa raíz (por ejemplo PLAT-7) y confirmar=False. Muestra la vista previa tal cual y pregunta si lo haces.
            | ESCALAR, PASO 2: solo si el usuario responde que sí a esa vista previa, llama {!@actions.EscalateBlockedCustomers} otra vez con los mismos valores y confirmar=True. Reporta los números de caso que devuelva. Si dice que no, no crees nada.
            | "AVÍSALE AL EQUIPO": el aviso al equipo son las tareas de seguimiento que crea la escalación para cada dueño de cuenta. Dilo así. Nunca digas que enviaste un mensaje, un correo o un aviso por Slack si no usaste una acción de Slack que lo haya enviado.
            | SOLO LO QUE HICISTE: reporta únicamente lo que las acciones devolvieron. Si algo no lo hizo una acción, no lo afirmes.
            | OPORTUNIDAD: para "¿nos alcanza?" o "¿dónde está la oportunidad?", usa {!@actions.FindProspects} con la región. Explica la brecha, por qué ese giro (go-lives más rápidos) y muestra los prospectos más cercanos. Aclara que son negocios reales de INEGI DENUE.
            | CREAR LEADS, PASO 1: si quieren crearlos, usa {!@actions.CreateProspectLeads} con los mismos criterios de la búsqueda y confirmar=False. Muestra la vista previa y pregunta.
            | CREAR LEADS, PASO 2: solo con un sí explícito, llama {!@actions.CreateProspectLeads} con los mismos criterios y confirmar=True.
            | RESUMEN PARA LA JUNTA: si piden bullets o un resumen para la junta, no llames acciones nuevas. Usa lo que ya devolvieron en esta conversación: diagnóstico, acciones tomadas (con números de caso) y plan. Máximo 3 viñetas. Si lo piden en un canvas de Slack, escribe el resumen y usa {!@actions.ir_a_slack} para crearlo.
            | Si una acción dice que falta la región o que no hay acceso, transmítelo y pregunta lo necesario. Nunca inventes datos.
        actions:
            ir_a_slack: @utils.transition to @subagent.Slack
            GetQuarterHealth: @actions.GetQuarterHealth
                with region = ...
                available when True
            GetRegionRisk: @actions.GetRegionRisk
                with region = ...
                available when True
            EscalateBlockedCustomers: @actions.EscalateBlockedCustomers
                with region = ...
                with blockerKey = ...
                with confirmar = ...
                available when True
            FindProspects: @actions.FindProspects
                with region = ...
                with family = ...
                with radiusKm = ...
                with maxResults = ...
                available when True
            CreateProspectLeads: @actions.CreateProspectLeads
                with region = ...
                with family = ...
                with radiusKm = ...
                with maxResults = ...
                with confirmar = ...
                available when True
    actions:
        GetQuarterHealth:
            description: "Avance del trimestre por región contra la meta, con datos en vivo del ERP (Snowflake vía Data Cloud Zero Copy)."
            label: "Revisar avance del trimestre"
            target: "apex://GetQuarterHealthAction"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Consultando el ERP"
            inputs:
                region: string
                    label: "Región"
                    description: "Opcional. Centro, Occidente, Norte o Península. Vacío = todas las regiones que el usuario puede ver."
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    is_displayable: False
            outputs:
                summary: string
                    label: "Resumen"
                    description: "Avance del trimestre por región: meta, reconocido, pronóstico y monto en riesgo."
                    developer_name: "summary"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        GetRegionRisk:
            description: "Causas raíz del retraso de una región: órdenes retrasadas del ERP cruzadas con bloqueos de Jira y casos de soporte abiertos."
            label: "Explicar riesgo de una región"
            target: "apex://GetRegionRiskAction"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Cruzando ERP, Jira y soporte"
            inputs:
                region: string
                    label: "Región"
                    description: "Centro, Occidente, Norte o Península. Por ejemplo 'Península'."
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    is_displayable: False
            outputs:
                summary: string
                    label: "Resumen"
                    description: "Causas raíz, clientes afectados, monto y casos de soporte abiertos."
                    developer_name: "summary"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        EscalateBlockedCustomers:
            description: "Escala a los clientes bloqueados por una incidencia de Jira. Con confirmar=False solo muestra la vista previa; con confirmar=True crea un caso por cliente y una tarea para cada dueño de cuenta."
            label: "Escalar clientes bloqueados"
            target: "apex://EscalateBlockedCustomersAction"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Preparando la escalación"
            inputs:
                region: string
                    label: "Región"
                    description: "Centro, Occidente, Norte o Península. Por ejemplo 'Península'."
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    is_displayable: False
                blockerKey: string
                    label: "Clave del bloqueo en Jira"
                    description: "La causa raíz a escalar, tal como la devolvió el análisis de riesgo. Por ejemplo 'PLAT-7'."
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    is_displayable: False
                confirmar: boolean
                    label: "Confirmado"
                    description: "False para la vista previa (no crea nada). True solo después de que el usuario dijo que sí a la vista previa."
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    is_displayable: False
            outputs:
                summary: string
                    label: "Resumen"
                    description: "Vista previa de la escalación o casos y tareas creados."
                    developer_name: "summary"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        FindProspects:
            description: "Brecha contra la meta, giro con go-lives más rápidos y negocios reales de INEGI DENUE cercanos a clientes actuales que aún no son Leads."
            label: "Buscar oportunidad en una región"
            target: "apex://FindProspectsAction"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Buscando en INEGI DENUE"
            inputs:
                region: string
                    label: "Región"
                    description: "Centro, Occidente, Norte o Península. Por ejemplo 'Península'."
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    is_displayable: False
                family: string
                    label: "Giro"
                    description: "Opcional: Farmacias, Restaurantes, Ferreterías o Abarrotes. Vacío = el giro con go-lives más rápidos en la región."
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    is_displayable: False
                radiusKm: number
                    label: "Radio en km"
                    description: "Opcional. Distancia máxima a un cliente actual. Por defecto 2."
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    is_displayable: False
                maxResults: object
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__integerType"
                    label: "Máximo de prospectos"
                    description: "Opcional. Por defecto 40."
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    is_displayable: False
            outputs:
                summary: string
                    label: "Resumen"
                    description: "Brecha, giro recomendado y prospectos más cercanos."
                    developer_name: "summary"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
        CreateProspectLeads:
            description: "Crea como Leads los prospectos encontrados, con los mismos criterios. Con confirmar=False solo muestra la vista previa; con confirmar=True los crea."
            label: "Crear prospectos como Leads"
            target: "apex://CreateProspectLeadsAction"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Preparando los Leads"
            inputs:
                region: string
                    label: "Región"
                    description: "La misma región de la búsqueda. Por ejemplo 'Península'."
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    is_displayable: False
                family: string
                    label: "Giro"
                    description: "El mismo giro de la búsqueda, o vacío si la búsqueda lo eligió sola."
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    is_displayable: False
                radiusKm: number
                    label: "Radio en km"
                    description: "El mismo radio de la búsqueda. Por defecto 2."
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    is_displayable: False
                maxResults: object
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__integerType"
                    label: "Máximo de prospectos"
                    description: "El mismo máximo de la búsqueda. Por defecto 40."
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    is_displayable: False
                confirmar: boolean
                    label: "Confirmado"
                    description: "False para la vista previa (no crea nada). True solo después de que el usuario dijo que sí."
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    is_displayable: False
            outputs:
                summary: string
                    label: "Resumen"
                    description: "Vista previa o Leads creados."
                    developer_name: "summary"
